1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
Europeans recycle more and they focus more on sustainability.
作者说，欧洲人回收得更多，也更重视可持续发展。

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:07,280
As you can see where you throw away your trash there's like different bins for different things.
你可以看到，丢垃圾的地方有不同的桶，分别收不同的东西。

3
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,359
And you'll see people actually following the rules.
而且你会看到，人们确实在遵守规则。

4
00:00:09,359 --> 00:00:15,280
And putting all the boxes here all the bottles in here and here for the trash.
把纸盒都放在这里，瓶子放在这里，这边放其他垃圾。

5
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:19,280
Just imagine how much cleaner the world would be if everybody followed europeans's lead on this.
想想看，如果每个人都在这方面效仿欧洲人，世界会干净多少。

6
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:23,599
In fact many european countries lead in renewable energy and eco friendly policies.
他说，事实上，许多欧洲国家在可再生能源和环保政策方面处于领先地位。

7
00:00:23,599 --> 00:00:26,229
Making these practices just a part of daily life.
这让这些做法成为日常生活的一部分。

8
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:30,310
It's normal for them to do these things they don't have to go out of their way because it's built into the culture.
对他们来说，这些做法很正常，不必特地费力，因为它已经融入文化。

9
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,960
The city is so clean even though there's so many tourists here.
这座城市很干净，尽管这里游客很多。

10
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,510
Because these amazing ladies that are just cleaning the city all day long.
因为这些了不起的女士们整天都在清洁城市。

11
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:38,560
Most european countries have strict rules on single use plastics.
他说，大多数欧洲国家对一次性塑料有严格规定。

12
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:42,800
Promote reusable items and have good public transportation that reduces car pollution.
鼓励可重复使用的物品，并有良好的公共交通来减少汽车污染。

13
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,310
Getting on the tram here beautiful old historic tram of Prague gives it all the charm in the world.
现在上电车，这辆美丽、古老的布拉格历史电车，真是魅力十足。

14
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:54,870
Green spaces in cities encourage outdoor activities and help improve air quality.
城市绿地鼓励户外活动，也有助于改善空气质量。

15
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:59,040
In the us let's just say that we don't care so much about recycling and it's really a shame.
至于美国，他觉得我们对回收没那么在意，这实在可惜。

16
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,880
This might be changing in recent generations.
近几代人的情况也许正在改变。

17
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:06,800
But even myself growing up we only recycled like big things like a cardboard box or a big carton of milk.
但连他自己小时候，也只回收纸箱、大牛奶盒之类的大件。

18
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,239
We didn't actually like collect everything separately and put it in different trash cans.
他们并没有把所有东西分开收集，放进不同的垃圾桶。

19
00:01:10,239 --> 00:01:13,359
We would just throw a water bottle in the same trash can that we would throw food waste.
水瓶会直接丢进同一个垃圾桶，食物垃圾也丢在那里。

20
00:01:13,359 --> 00:01:16,239
In the us I see a lot of people littering and not taking care of the streets.
他在美国看到很多人乱扔垃圾，也不爱护街道。

21
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:22,160
And for such a big country with 350 million people you can imagine the massive impact that it has on the world.
对于一个有三亿五千万人口的大国，你能想象这会对世界产生多大影响。

22
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,680
I will say that some places in the us do put recycling forward.
他也承认，美国有些地方确实把回收摆在前面。

23
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:30,000
But overall as a society as a nation I think we are light years behind Europe.
但总体作为一个社会、一个国家，他觉得美国比欧洲落后太远。

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,839
And this might not be a problem for us in today's world but for our kids generation it's detrimental recycle please.
这对我们今天也许还不是问题，但对孩子那一代有害。所以，请回收。

25
00:01:35,839 --> 00:01:39,910
We do care about earth.
我们确实关心地球。

26
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:45,040
Many americans dress really casually like myself baseball cap regular shirt or athletic shirts.
许多美国人穿得很休闲，就像他：棒球帽、普通上衣或运动上衣。

27
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,560
I'm wearing yoga shorts right now.
他现在穿的就是瑜伽短裤。

28
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:49,599
A lot of americans love to rep their universities or their sporting teams.
很多美国人喜欢用服装展示对母校或球队的支持。

29
00:01:49,599 --> 00:01:53,440
And that's just how we are you know hoodies regular shoes socks shorts.
他说，我们就是这样，连帽衫、普通鞋子、袜子、短裤。

30
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:55,119
Europeans on the other hand are really fancy.
而在他看来，欧洲人则打扮得很讲究。

31
00:01:55,119 --> 00:01:59,280
And when they dress up to go to dinners and to go out and just to like whenever they leave their house.
他们打扮好去吃晚饭、外出，甚至可以说，只要离开家——

32
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:04,080
Even if they go to the grocery store they just present themselves nicer and they have fancier haircuts and they're more elegant looking.
即使去超市，也会把自己收拾得更好，发型更讲究，看起来更优雅。

33
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:07,680
And personally I feel a little bit um like an outsider in some situations.
就他自己而言，在有些情境中，他会有点像个局外人。

34
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:13,200
When I go sit outside on a cafe and everyone's looking nice and I'm just there like clearly there's an american dude that shows up.
在咖啡馆外坐下，大家都打扮得很好，而他一出现，就明显是个美国哥们。

35
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:18,479
But this is usually how they can pick out americans from the crowd in any city in the world is like how they dress.
他说，通常在世界任何城市，人们都能通过穿着从人群里认出美国人。

36
00:02:18,479 --> 00:02:22,800
Everything's so posh and fancy here I feel like I stand out wearing my be spontaneous shirt.
这里的一切都那么时髦讲究，他穿着印有“随性一点”的上衣，觉得自己很显眼。

37
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:27,440
We stumbled upon a wedding and I don't think we fit in very well everyone's dressed super nicely.
他们偶然遇到一场婚礼；他觉得自己不太融入，因为大家都穿得特别漂亮。

38
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,080
This is also reflected in the workplace in the work environment.
这种区别也体现在职场、工作环境中。

39
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:33,920
Where in the us a lot of companies are more casual with like jeans and just a regular shirt.
美国许多公司更随意，比如穿牛仔裤和普通上衣。

40
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:37,920
Whereas in Europe they take fashion more seriously and people have to dress up look nicer.
而在他看来，欧洲更重视时尚，人们得打扮得更好看。

41
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,520
And hey there's nothing wrong with looking nice.
嘿，打扮得好看当然没什么不好。

42
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:43,760
You know there might be many americans watching this out there that really like looking nice and that's awesome.
他知道，也许有不少正在看视频的美国人就很喜欢打扮，那也很好。

43
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:47,599
But I'm just saying overall as a society europeans care a lot more about their looks.
不过他只是想说，总体作为一个社会，他觉得欧洲人更在意外表。

44
00:02:47,599 --> 00:02:53,200
Random side note this tower called jishkov tower in Prague is a really awkward looking building.
顺带说一句，布拉格这座他称作 jishkov 的塔，看起来很奇特。〔塔名识别待复核〕

45
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:58,839
And you can see there's black babies going up and down the side of it right there really really weird and funky.
你可以看到，塔身侧面有黑色婴儿造型上下攀爬，那里，很古怪，也很别致。〔指外墙雕塑〕

46
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:04,870
Let's look in this circle for example all the houses are really nice and neat.
再看看这个环形区域，房屋都很漂亮、整洁。

47
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:08,229
Most of them are just apartments the buildings are right next to each other.
大部分就是公寓，楼房彼此紧挨着。

48
00:03:08,239 --> 00:03:10,160
Everything's kind of laid out perfectly nicely.
所有东西的布局似乎都恰到好处。

49
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:13,440
There's plazas people are reading in the park sitting in their little chairs.
有广场，有人在公园读书，坐在小椅子里。

50
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:17,280
It almost feels like a fake life like you would see in a movie like a giant movie set.
这几乎像一种不真实的生活，像电影里看到的，像一个巨大的电影布景。

51
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:22,719
That's how it feels here in most of Europe wow that is so cool and it's nice.
他说，欧洲大部分地方给他的感觉就是如此。哇，真酷，也很舒服。

52
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:27,200
It's nice to hang out walk around and sit down it's freaking beautiful.
在这里待着、散步、坐一坐都很好，真是美极了。

53
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:31,030
A lot of the buildings are really old they've been here for many years and that's just how they are.
许多建筑很古老，已经在这里很多年，它们就是保留着这样的样子。
